- If TD Ameritrade activity includes sales of securities with gains/losses, you may need Form 8949 and Schedule D (capital gains).

8. Qualified Business Income (QBI) deduction
- You may be eligible for a QBI (Section 199A) deduction of up to 20% of qualified business income from your Schedule C (subject to rules/thresholds). With relatively modest net self‑employment income, you are likely eligible for some QBI deduction; calculation can be done when preparing the return. This is another reason to ensure you report Schedule C accurately.

9. Estimated tax / withholding
- With $12,500 self‑employment, you will owe self‑employment tax and possibly additional income tax. If your W‑2 withholdings cover it, you may be fine; otherwise consider quarterly estimated payments for future years.

Forms you’ll likely need (federal)
- Form 1040 (U.S. Individual Income Tax Return)
- Schedule 1 (Additional Income and Adjustments) — for some adjustments (student loan interest, etc.)
- Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business) — to report consulting income and business expenses
