- Schedule A (Itemized Deductions) — only if you itemize
- Form 8995 (or 8995-A) if you claim the QBI deduction (Form used depends on income/complexity)
- Form 1040-ES (estimated tax vouchers) — if you need to make quarterly estimated payments during the year

State (Arizona)
- Arizona Form 140 (individual income tax return) — Arizona will require reporting of income; most items generally flow from federal return but check state-specific adjustments and credits.
- Arizona also has its own rules for deductions/credits; if you withhold state tax from wages, that will be reported and used on your AZ return.

Recordkeeping checklist
- W-2(s), 1099-NEC, 1099-INT
- 1098-E for student loan interest
- Charity receipts / acknowledgments
- Rent receipts / canceled checks, utility bills, renter’s insurance statements (for home-office allocation)
- Record of business expenses and dates; mileage log if you used a vehicle for business
- Documentation of square footage and how you measured the office

Quick examples (illustrative only)
- If you use the regular home-office allocation (≈20.29% of rent) you could claim about $5,100 for the office portion of rent; if your consulting net income (after other business expenses) is large enough, that reduces taxable income more than the simplified $700 method.
- Student loan interest: from $3,600 paid, you can typically deduct up to $2,500 (subject to income limits). Confirm the year the interest was paid and the 1098-E.

Questions I have for you
