- Deductible half of SE tax ≈ $765 (above-the-line)

Student loan interest:
- You can deduct up to $2,500 (if you qualify based on MAGI); this reduces your AGI further.

Qualified Business Income (QBI) deduction:
- You may be eligible for up to 20% of QBI (roughly 20% × net business income after adjustments). With relatively low business income you will likely qualify for some or all of the QBI deduction — that would further reduce taxable income. QBI rules have limits for higher-income taxpayers and special rules for service businesses; I can estimate this more precisely if you want.

Bottom line about taxes owed:
- You will owe self-employment tax on net consulting profit (~$1.5k in my rough calc) in addition to regular income tax. Half of that SE tax is deductible.
- Because you have substantial W-2 withholding, your total income tax might be mostly covered by withholding, but you may owe an additional amount for SE tax and any income tax shortfall. If you expect taxes owed > $1,000 after withholding, you should make estimated tax payments or increase W-4 withholding to cover it.

