5. Do you have any mortgage interest, property tax, large state‑income tax payments, or other itemizable expenses that you didn’t mention?

Caveats
- I’m not a CPA or tax attorney. This is general guidance based on current law through mid‑2024. Exact phaseout thresholds (student loan interest MAGI limits, standard deduction amounts, etc.) should be confirmed with current IRS tables or a tax preparer. If you want, I can run a more precise estimate of your 2024 federal tax (with calculations) if you confirm the clarifying items above and any other deductions/withholdings.

