  - Subtract half SE tax and student loan interest ($2,500) from income to get AGI
  - After AGI, standard deduction $29,200 likely yields lower taxable income than itemizing
- Estimated taxes: since you have self-employment income, you may owe estimated taxes or need to increase withholding on your W‑2 job to avoid underpayment penalties. If you expect to owe >$1,000 when you file, consider making estimated payments or adjusting withholding.
- Documentation: keep receipts for the $1,400 charitable gift (required for contributions > $250), proof of home-office exclusivity (floor plan / photos can help if ever needed), receipts for business expenses, and Form 1098‑E from MOHELA for student loan interest.

8) Next steps I recommend
- Confirm the two clarifying items I asked about (student loan interest year, nature of the $950).
