2) Home office — two methods and calculations
You can choose either the simplified method or the actual-expense method:

- Simplified method: $5 per square foot × 140 sq ft = $700 deduction (max 300 sq ft).
  - Advantage: easy, no Form 8829.
  - Effect: reduces Schedule C net profit by $700.

- Actual expense method: apportion rent and allowable expenses by the business percentage (exclusive, regular use required). You gave rent = $2,100/mo = $25,200/yr.
  - Business percent = 140 / 690 ≈ 20.29%.
  - Rent portion deductible = $25,200 × 20.29% ≈ $5,116.
