  - You would use Form 8829 (Expenses for Business Use of Your Home) to compute this if using actual-expense method.

Which to choose here? With rent at $25,200/yr the actual method looks far more beneficial (≈$5,116 vs $700). Use actual method if you can document rent and utilities.

3) Self-employment tax, QBI, and business expenses
- Report the consulting income and business expenses on Schedule C. If the $950 “unreimbursed expenses” are business expenses for the consulting, they belong on Schedule C (not Schedule A).
