- Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business) — report consulting income and business expenses (including home-office deduction if you claim it here)
- Schedule SE (Self-Employment Tax)
- Form 8829 (Expenses for Business Use of Your Home) — only if you use the actual method to calculate the home-office deduction. If you use the simplified method ($5/sqft), you do not file Form 8829.
- Form(s) 1099-INT and/or 1099-DIV — include bank/broker interest and dividends. If you have a 1099-NEC for any client paying $600+, include it on Schedule C (but you must report self-employment income even without a 1099).
- Schedule A (Itemized Deductions) — only if you choose to itemize.
- State return: Arizona individual return (AZ Form 140 or whichever AZ form applies for 2024) — follow state rules for deductions and adjustments. Arizona tax treatment may differ slightly (confirm with AZ instructions or a preparer).

