3) Home office deduction (applies only to the self‑employment activity)
You have a dedicated 140 sq ft exclusive home office in a 690 sq ft home:
- Business percentage = 140 / 690 ≈ 20.29%.

Two methods:
- Simplified: $5 per sq ft × 140 = $700 (max 300 sq ft).
- Actual method: prorate actual home expenses (rent, utilities, insurance, repairs, etc.). Example using rent only: annual rent = $2,100 × 12 = $25,200. Deductible portion = $25,200 × 20.29% ≈ $5,114. You would also prorate utilities and other qualifying expenses, which raises the deduction further.

