- The home office deduction cannot exceed the net income from that business (gross receipts minus other business expenses) for that year. If your consulting net is $12,500 minus other business expenses, the home office deduction is most likely allowable. If the deduction would create a Schedule C loss, some limits may apply — but usually you can take it up to net profit.
