  b) Regular (actual) method: allocate a percentage of actual home expenses to the business. Your business percentage = 140 / 690 ≈ 20.3%. You may allocate 20.3% of rent, utilities, renter’s insurance, repairs, etc., to the business. For rent only: annual rent = $2,100 * 12 = $25,200 → 20.3% × $25,200 ≈ $5,111. Add proportional utilities/insurance/repairs if applicable. Note: the actual method requires Form 8829.
