- If for consulting (self‑employed), include on Schedule C.
- If these are unreimbursed employee expenses for your W‑2 job, they are not deductible for 2018–2025.

5) Standard deduction vs. itemizing
- 2024 standard deduction for married filing jointly (estimate) is substantially larger than $1,400 in charitable gifts, so you will almost certainly take the standard deduction unless you also have mortgage interest, large state/local taxes (up to $10k cap), or additional big medical expenses. Home office does NOT require itemizing (it is a Schedule C deduction).

6) Qualified Business Income (QBI) deduction
- You may be eligible for a 20% QBI deduction (Section 199A) on qualified business income from your consulting (Form 8995 or 8995‑A). With your income ranges, you should be under the thresholds that complicate the calculation, so you could get up to 20% of your net business income. That makes maximizing legitimate Schedule C deductions (like the home office share) even more helpful.

7) Forms you will generally need
