A. What you can likely deduct (federal)
- W-2 wages: $79,400 — reported on Form 1040 (W-2).
- Self‑employment/consulting income: $12,500 — report on Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business). Business expenses (see below) reduce this.
  - If the $950 “unreimbursed expenses” are business expenses for your consulting work, they are deductible on Schedule C. If they are unreimbursed employee expenses for a W-2 job, they are NOT deductible (suspended by TCJA).
