- Charitable contributions: $1,400 to Northwest Harvest with receipt — deductible if you itemize (Schedule A). If you take the standard deduction, you cannot also deduct this on Schedule A.
- Self‑employment tax: You pay self‑employment tax (Social Security + Medicare) on net Schedule C income — calculated on Schedule SE. One half of SE tax is deductible as an adjustment to income on Schedule 1.

B. Itemize vs standard deduction (quick assessment)
- 2024 standard deduction for Married Filing Jointly: $29,200.
- Known potential itemized amounts you listed: $1,400 charitable. You didn’t list mortgage interest, large state or local taxes, or big medical expenses, so your obvious itemizable deductions are small compared with $29,200.
