     b) Actual expenses: allocate actual home expenses by office percentage. Your office % = 140/690 ≈ 20.29%. Example using rent only: annual rent $25,200 × 20.29% ≈ $5,113. (You could also allocate utilities, renter’s insurance, etc. — all prorated by the percentage.)
   - Choose the method that gives the larger deduction (actual often gives more when rent is substantial). The home office deduction reduces Schedule C net profit, which reduces both income tax and self-employment tax.

