Other practical items and recommendations
- Keep all receipts and documentation: charity receipts, student loan 1098‑E (or statements showing interest paid), 1099‑NEC/1099‑MISC/1099‑INT/1099‑DIV as issued by payers, records of rent, utilities, and how you measured the office space.
- Make sure the $3,600 student-loan interest amount reflects payments made in the filing year. If payments were made in prior years, they’re not deductible on this year’s return.
- If you expect to owe tax because of self-employment income (including self-employment tax), consider estimated tax payments quarterly to avoid penalties (Form 1040‑ES).
