- Home office deduction = 140 sq ft × $5 = $700
- Other business expenses (assume the $950 are business expenses) = $950
- Total business expenses = 1,650 → Net self‑employment income = 12,500 − 1,650 = 10,850
- Net subject to SE tax (multiply by 0.9235) ≈ 10,850 × 0.9235 ≈ 10,022
- Self‑employment tax ≈ 10,022 × 15.3% ≈ $1,533 → half deductible ≈ $767

